# node
node_modules/
frontend/dist/

# LLM response cache -- COMMITTED ON PURPOSE since the Render deploy.
#
# It used to be ignored, on the reasoning that it regenerates. That reasoning
# holds on a laptop and fails on a free Render instance: .cache is written at
# RUNTIME, and a free instance restarts from the built image on every wake, so
# a warmed cache is gone after fifteen idle minutes and the demo pays full
# provider latency again (measured live: 9-24s a call).
#
# Committing it makes the warm cache part of the BUILD, so every cold start,
# every redeploy and every wake begins with the rehearsed answers already in
# hand. cache.py keys on sha256(system + prompt + schema) -- no machine, no
# provider, no model -- so a cache warmed on a laptop is valid on Render.
#
# Safe to commit: an entry stores only the response ({text, provider, model}).
# The prompt, which carries the retrieved textbook context, is never written to
# disk -- it only exists as the filename hash. The books stay ignored below.
#
# Cost: local runs add entries, so it shows up in git status. Worth it until
# the event; re-ignore afterwards if the noise annoys anyone.

# models / large artefacts
backend/data/*.pdf
# source material: large, and usually someone else's copyright. The manifest
# is committed so the team can see what the corpus is made of; the books are not.
backend/data/pdfs/*
!backend/data/.gitkeep
!backend/data/pdfs/.gitkeep
!backend/data/pdfs/manifest.json
*.safetensors
*.bin

# os
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store

# claude code local settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# frontend build artefacts
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
frontend/dist/

# local dev harness -- throwaway test UI, never pushed (see dev-harness/README.md)
dev-harness/
backend_run.log
backend_run.err.log

# embedding model, pre-fetched by render-build.sh (see render.yaml)
.fastembed_cache/
